{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Record sudo commands on node1 in /var/log/sudo-commands.log with the invoking user and timestamp.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed sudoers policy directs sudo to the dedicated logfile and passes syntax validation. Direct probes before and after restart produced entries containing timestamps, invoking user antrieb, target user root, and the executed command. The logfile is root-owned and mode 0600.","evidence_ids":["cmd-043aa9293baf4d8c","cmd-1925528f11f04a7a","cmd-a50aeff2c02c4201","cmd-940257a8cb5f4139"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep sudo command entries out of the general system log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The policy disables sudo syslog output. Unique pre- and post-restart probes appeared in the dedicated logfile while searches of /var/log/messages, /var/log/secure, and the systemd journal each returned zero matches.","evidence_ids":["cmd-043aa9293baf4d8c","cmd-1925528f11f04a7a","cmd-940257a8cb5f4139"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after execution, node1 remained RHEL Server 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64. The implementation used the already installed RHEL 7 sudo 1.8.23 functionality, with no package or kernel replacement shown.","evidence_ids":["cmd-caabe670d9b947f1","cmd-ad5b691a718043f7","cmd-940257a8cb5f4139","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"The functional mutations—the sudoers policy, protected logfile, bounded probes, and mandatory restart—have clear task or evidence roles. The sole unnecessary residue is /tmp/99-sudo-command-logging, created by cmd-043aa9293baf4d8c as a staging file but not removed; it remained after execution. No failed services or new listening exposure appeared. The restart protocol is strong: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged reboot, observed stopping and temporary loss of access, a different boot ID, and recovered system, rsyslog, policy, retained data, and post-restart behavior; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree.","evidence_ids":["cmd-043aa9293baf4d8c","cmd-ad5b691a718043f7","cmd-b73c3dcc1ff04287","cmd-5187d18825154435","cmd-9c23fe988a8147b8","cmd-964f27b34e7b4ed4","cmd-940257a8cb5f4139","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence, including persistence and isolation after a verified node restart. The only notable hygiene issue is one abandoned low-risk staging file in /tmp.","limitations":["Package-manager consistency checks timed out both before and after execution, so package health could not be independently assessed.","The universal claim that every future sudo command will be recorded is necessarily inferred from the validated global sudo policy plus representative pre- and post-restart probes rather than exhaustive testing of every possible command path."]}
